# Release Notes Integration Flow

This sequence diagram illustrates how the Support Microservice retrieves release notes directly from **GitHub’s Releases API**, caches them, and exposes them to the UI dashboard.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant ADMIN as Admin / User
    participant UI as Support UI (Dashboard)
    participant API as API Gateway
    participant SVC as Support Microservice
    participant GITHUB as GitHub Releases API
    participant CACHE as Redis Cache (optional)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (metadata cache)

    ADMIN->>UI: Open "Release Notes" Page
    UI->>API: GET /support/releases
    API->>SVC: Forward Request (Fetch Releases)

    alt Cache Hit
        SVC->>CACHE: Check Cached Releases
        CACHE-->>SVC: Cached Release Data Found
    else Cache Miss
        SVC->>GITHUB: GET /repos/{org}/{repo}/releases (via GitHub API)
        GITHUB-->>SVC: JSON Response (Latest Releases)
        SVC->>CACHE: Store Release Data (TTL 1h)
        SVC->>DB: Optionally persist metadata (version, date, notes summary)
    end

    SVC-->>API: Return Parsed Release Notes
    API-->>UI: Render Latest Release Notes List
    Note over UI,ADMIN: User sees version, title, description, and published date
